<!--meta {"lead": "A table compares many records across the same columns: requests by date, status and estimate. On HairPop it is the dense alternative to row cards, for people who manage several appointments.", "description": "Default, dense, sortable, selectable and row-action tables with caption, sticky header, loading, empty and error states, scrolling inside a wrapper on phones.", "pills": ["Native <code>&lt;table&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "default, dense, sortable, selectable, with row actions, sticky header; responsive scroll or cards", "states": "default, row hover, row focus-within, row selected, sorted, loading, empty, error", "sources": []} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a table when people compare or scan many records with the same fields: appointment history, payouts, review moderation. Use row cards (<code>.appointment-row</code>) when there are only a few records or each needs a sentence of context, as on My appointments today. Use a <a href="description-list.html">description list</a> for the fields of one record. Never use a table for layout.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Default</b>: 12 × 16px cells, sunken sticky header.</li>
    <li><b>Dense</b> (<code>.table--dense</code>): 8 × 12px cells for long histories.</li>
    <li><b>Sortable</b>: header buttons with <code>aria-sort</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Selectable</b>: a checkbox column and a bulk action bar.</li>
    <li><b>With row actions</b>: actions appear on hover or focus, always visible on touch.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <div class="table-wrap" style="width: 100%;"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Date</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">HP-1048</th><td>Sat 24 Oct</td><td class="num">$180–$240</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 10%; top: 24%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 10%; top: 48%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 40%; top: 72%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 80%; top: 72%;" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Caption</b><small>Names the table; label type; can be visually hidden when a heading sits above.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Header row</b><small><code>&lt;th scope="col"&gt;</code>, label type in <code>--color-fg-muted</code> on <code>--color-bg-surface-sunken</code>; sticky.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Row header and cells</b><small>The identifying cell is <code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code> in label type on the row's own background; cells have <code>--space-3</code> × <code>--space-4</code> padding, body-sm type, one line each, and a hairline row divider.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Numeric cell</b><small><code>.num</code>: right-aligned, tabular figures.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  <h3>Default with sort and row actions</h3>
  {{example:[stack]Date is sorted descending; Estimate is sortable but unsorted (no <code>aria-sort</code>, no arrow); row actions show on hover and focus. On a phone the table scrolls inside its wrapper, which is then a named, focusable region.}}
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="table">
    <caption>Your appointments</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col" aria-sort="descending"><button type="button">Date</button></th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col" class="num"><button type="button">Estimate</button></th><th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">HP-1048</th><td>Medium knotless braids</td><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am</td><td><span class="badge badge--warning">Awaiting reply</span></td><td class="num">$180–$240</td><td><div class="row-actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">View HP-1048</a></div></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">HP-0992</th><td>Medium knotless braids</td><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Sat 3 Oct · 9:30 am</td><td><span class="badge">Completed</span></td><td class="num">$210</td><td><div class="row-actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="../../mocks/pages/care-and-review/default.html">Review HP-0992</a></div></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Selectable and dense</h3>
  {{example:[stack]A checkbox column with a bulk action bar; dense padding for long histories.}}
<div class="cluster cluster--between"><span class="text-muted">1 selected</span><button class="btn btn--sm" type="button">Download receipts</button></div>
<div class="table-wrap">
  <table class="table table--dense">
    <caption class="visually-hidden">Past appointments</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col"><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox"><span class="visually-hidden">Select all appointments</span></label></th><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col" class="num">Paid</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr aria-selected="true"><td><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" checked><span class="visually-hidden">Select HP-0992</span></label></td><th scope="row">HP-0992</th><td>Nia Okafor</td><td class="num">$210</td></tr>
      <tr><td><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox"><span class="visually-hidden">Select HP-0911</span></label></td><th scope="row">HP-0911</th><td>Aisha Mensah</td><td class="num">$195</td></tr>
      <tr><td><label class="choice"><input type="checkbox"><span class="visually-hidden">Select HP-0874</span></label></td><th scope="row">HP-0874</th><td>Jules Baptiste</td><td class="num">$170</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes"><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Medium (default) 12 × 16px cells; small (<code>.table--dense</code>) 8 × 12px cells.}}
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption class="visually-hidden">Medium table</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Medium</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">HP-1048</th><td class="num">$180–$240</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table table--dense"><caption class="visually-hidden">Small table</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Small</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">HP-1048</th><td class="num">$180–$240</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Rows highlight on hover and while a control inside has focus; the row header takes the same tint as its row; selected rows use the accent tint; sorted columns show an arrow and <code>aria-sort</code>. The table as a whole can be loading, empty or in error.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table">
      <caption>Row states</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col"><span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Default</td><th scope="row">HP-1048</th><td>Nia Okafor</td><td><div class="row-actions"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button">View</button></div></td></tr>
        <tr data-state="hover"><td>Hover</td><th scope="row">HP-0992</th><td>Nia Okafor</td><td><div class="row-actions"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button">View</button></div></td></tr>
        <tr data-state="hover"><td>Focus within</td><th scope="row">HP-0911</th><td>Aisha Mensah</td><td><div class="row-actions"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-state="focus">View</button></div></td></tr>
        <tr data-state="selected"><td>Selected</td><th scope="row">HP-0874</th><td>Jules Baptiste</td><td><div class="row-actions"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button">View</button></div></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h3>Loading, empty and error</h3>
  {{example:[stack]Loading keeps the header and shows skeleton rows; empty and error states replace the body with one row.}}
<div class="table-wrap" aria-busy="true"><table class="table"><caption>Loading appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class="skeleton skeleton--text" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="skeleton skeleton--text" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="skeleton skeleton--text" aria-hidden="true"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class="skeleton skeleton--text" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="skeleton skeleton--text" aria-hidden="true"></span></td><td><span class="skeleton skeleton--text" aria-hidden="true"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>No appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="3"><div class="empty empty--compact"><p class="empty__title">No appointments yet</p><p class="empty__text">When you request a visit, you’ll find its status here.</p></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments failed to load</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="3"><div class="empty empty--compact empty--error"><p class="empty__title">We couldn’t load your appointments</p><p class="empty__text">Check your connection and try again.</p><div class="empty__actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Try again</button></div></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes:stack}}<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption class="visually-hidden">Theme sample</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col" class="num">Estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">HP-1048</th><td><span class="badge badge--warning">Awaiting reply</span></td><td class="num">$180–$240</td></tr><tr data-state="hover"><th scope="row">HP-0992</th><td><span class="badge">Completed</span></td><td class="num">$210</td></tr><tr data-state="selected"><th scope="row">HP-0911</th><td><span class="badge">Completed</span></td><td class="num">$195</td></tr></tbody></table></div>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The table scrolls horizontally inside <code>.table-wrap</code>; the page never scrolls sideways. Keep the identifying column first so it is visible before scrolling.</li>
    <li>Below 768px, a table with four columns or fewer may switch to row cards (<code>.card.appointment-row</code>) when the screen says so; My appointments uses cards at every width today.</li>
    <li>Row actions are always visible under <code>(hover: none)</code>.</li>
    <li>Cell values stay on one line (<code>white-space: nowrap</code>), so a column is as wide as its longest value and a wide table scrolls inside the wrapper instead of breaking "Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am" over several lines. A full-width empty or error row wraps.</li>
    <li>While the table overflows, the wrapper is a focusable region named by the caption (<code>role="region"</code>, <code>aria-labelledby</code>, <code>tabindex="0"</code>) so keyboard users can scroll it; when it fits, it carries none of these.</li>
    <li>The column header row is sticky only inside the wrapper's own scroll area. The wrapper scrolls horizontally only, so on the page the header scrolls away with the table: paginate long histories rather than nesting a vertical scroll area.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The table reads <code>--color-bg-surface</code> (wrapper), <code>--color-bg-surface-sunken</code> (header), <code>--color-border-default</code> (rules), <code>--color-bg-subtle</code> (hover) and <code>--color-accent-subtle</code> (selected). Dark theme keeps the same roles: a grey 925 header on a grey 900 body.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>A native <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;caption&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;th scope="col"&gt;</code> and a row header (<code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code>) for the identifying cell; see the <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/table/">APG Table pattern</a>. Sortable headers contain a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> and the <code>&lt;th&gt;</code> carries <code>aria-sort</code>. It is not a grid widget: cells are not focusable, only the controls in them.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Moves through sort buttons, checkboxes and row actions in order; focus within a row reveals its actions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd> / <kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Sorts by the focused column; toggles a checkbox; activates a row action.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd> with the wrapper focused</td><td>Scrolls a wide table horizontally; the overflowing wrapper is a tab stop.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared ring on the overflowing wrapper, sort buttons and row controls. Sort buttons look like header text but keep a 24px (<code>--target-min</code>) target. A row with focus inside gets the hover tint so the row being acted on is visible. In forced colours a selected row gets a <code>Highlight</code> inset outline, because the system removes its tint.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The caption names the table. Row actions name their record ("View HP-1048"), and row checkboxes name theirs ("Select HP-0992"). An empty header over actions has visually hidden text "Actions". Loading tables set <code>aria-busy="true"</code> on the wrapper; skeletons are <code>aria-hidden</code>.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Header label on header|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface-sunken|4.5}}
    {{pair:Cell text|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Cell text on hover row|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Cell text on selected row|--color-fg-default|--color-accent-subtle|4.5}}
    {{pair:Checkbox edge|--color-border-strong|--color-bg-surface|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Row actions fade in over <code>--duration-fast</code>; reduced motion makes it instant. Skeleton shimmer pauses under reduced motion.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Row actions are small buttons (32px) separated by at least 8px and always visible on touch; checkboxes sit in a 24px target.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Column headers are nouns in sentence case ("Request", "Braider", "Estimate").</li>
    <li>Dates read "Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am"; money is right-aligned with tabular figures; ranges use an en dash ("$180–$240").</li>
    <li>Status is a badge with text, never colour alone.</li>
    <li>Empty and error rows follow the empty-state formula: what is missing, why, and one action.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="card appointment-row"><div><span class="badge badge--warning">Awaiting reply</span><p><b>Nia Okafor · knotless braids</b></p></div><button class="btn btn--sm" type="button">View request</button></div></div><figcaption>With two or three records, keep the row cards My appointments uses.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption class="visually-hidden">Layout misuse</caption><tbody><tr><td><b>Nia Okafor</b></td><td><button class="btn btn--sm" type="button">View</button></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><figcaption>Use a table to lay out one card's contents.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">View HP-1048</a></div><figcaption>Name the record in row actions.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">View</a><a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">View</a></div><figcaption>Repeat identical "View" links; a screen-reader link list cannot tell them apart.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Body background|--color-bg-surface}}
      {{tok:Header background|--color-bg-surface-sunken}}
      {{tok:Header label|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Row rule, wrapper edge|--color-border-default}}
      {{tok:Row hover|--color-bg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Row selected|--color-accent-subtle}}
      {{tok:Cell padding (default)|--space-3|--space-4}}
      {{tok:Cell padding (dense)|--space-2|--space-3}}
      {{tok:Cell font, header font|--text-body-sm|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Wrapper radius|--radius-lg}}
      {{tok:Row actions fade|--duration-fast}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;div class="table-wrap"&gt;
  &lt;table class="table"&gt;
    &lt;caption&gt;Your appointments&lt;/caption&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col"&gt;Request&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col" aria-sort="descending"&gt;&lt;button type="button"&gt;Date&lt;/button&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col" class="num"&gt;Estimate&lt;/th&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;th scope="row"&gt;HP-1048&lt;/th&gt;&lt;td&gt;Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td class="num"&gt;$180–$240&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;
  &lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.table-wrap</code></td><td>Bordered, rounded, horizontally scrolling container.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.table</code> <code>.table--dense</code></td><td>Base table; compact padding.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.num</code></td><td>Right-aligned tabular figures.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>&lt;button&gt;</code> in a <code>thead th</code></td><td>Sortable header: header text look, 24px target, shared focus ring.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-sort="ascending|descending"</code></td><td>On the sorted column only; adds the decorative arrow.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code></td><td>Row header: label type, row's own background.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-selected="true"</code> on <code>tr</code></td><td>Selected row tint.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.row-actions</code></td><td>Actions revealed on hover and focus, always shown on touch.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|selected"</code> on <code>tr</code></td><td>Documentation only: forces a row state.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Core-set component: no mock uses a table yet. The data it would hold appears as row cards in:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/my-appointments/default|two appointments as row cards}}
    {{mock:pages/my-appointments/long|paged list of 126 results, where a dense table would help}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: none in the mocks; the kit's sort arrows were typed glyphs that screen readers announced (now hidden with empty alt text in <code>content</code>), and row actions had no record names. Fixed in the stylesheet: row headers were painted like column headers (sunken, muted, sticky), so hover and selection stopped at the first cell; the last row's row header kept its rule; unsorted sort buttons kept the browser's button style and sorted ones were 23px tall; values wrapped over several lines on phones.</p>
</section>
